{"t": 1794117252.6099017, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "[checkout] PaymentGatewayErrors (AG-7731) \u2014 root cause found and fixed in code.\n\nWhat happened: the payment gateway moved to API version 2026-11, which requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents). checkout/gateway.py was still sending decimal euros, so charges were rejected.\n\nEvidence: Loki app=checkout at 07:41:03Z \u2014 `WARN gateway rejected charge status=400 body={\"error\":\"invalid_amount\",\"message\":\"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\"}` followed by `INFO gateway api version switched to 2026-11 (strict amounts)`. Matches the 38% gateway 4xx rate since 07:41 UTC.\n\nFix: charge_payload() now converts EUR to integer cents (Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP) before sending; verified 12.34 -> 1234. Needs deploy to clear the 4xx rate.\n\nNo Sentry errors were recorded for this (gateway 4xx are handled responses).\n"}, "ok": true}
